WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.534
Picture one bartender, and a line that wraps around the planet.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.878
Everyone asks about their job, their ex, their hair.

3
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.391
The advice is good, so everyone takes it.

4
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:12.644
Six months later, the whole town has the same haircut.

5
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:14.366
Every dog is named Biscuit.

6
00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:16.967
Every breakup text says, I've really grown.

7
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:20.284
A real study found something similar.

8
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:24.212
Writers given AI ideas wrote better stories, but more alike.

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.875
Sameness can be costly. Just ask the banana.

10
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.332
Most bananas sold abroad were one clone, the Gros Michel.

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.100
Then a fungus hit, and by the 1960s that trade collapsed.

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.732
Its replacement, the Cavendish, is also a clone.

13
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.021
And a new strain of that fungus is spreading.

14
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.268
To be fair, sometimes agreeing is good.

15
00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.882
Nobody needs a hot take on seatbelts or soap.

16
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.656
Full disclosure: I'm the bartender, so I'm the worst judge here.

17
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:56.747
When millions ask one AI for advice, opinions may drift closer.

18
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:59.277
Is that a loss even when the advice is good?

19
00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.129
Or only when we're all wrong together?

20
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.679
Here, take a napkin. It says: get a second opinion, not from me.
